    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Quillsen are delighted to introduce to the market this elegant three-bedroom detached residence, dating from the 1920`s and occupying a highly coveted position in one of Clontarf`s premier residential locations.\n\nA home of considerable charm and character, the property has been extended over the years and offers well-balanced accommodation together with exceptional scope for further enhancement. Of particular note is the substantial garage to the side, which extends the full length of the property and presents an exciting opportunity for further development or conversion, subject to the necessary planning permission.\n\nBehind its attractive period façade, the accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hall with guest WC, gracious sitting room, dining room/family room, kitchen/breakfast room, three bedrooms and a family bathroom. The existing accommodation provides a superb foundation from which to create a truly exceptional family home, while the generous footprint offers considerable flexibility for the future.\n\nThe mature gardens are a particular feature of the property. The front garden provides a pleasant approach, while to the rear lies a wonderful private garden enjoying a highly desirable southerly aspect. Bathed in natural light, this is an ideal space for outdoor entertaining, relaxation and family enjoyment, with considerable scope for further landscaping and enhancement.\n\nThe location is quite simply outstanding. Clontarf is renowned for its village atmosphere, coastal setting and exceptional range of amenities, and this property is ideally placed to enjoy all that the area has to offer. Clontarf Village is within easy reach, providing an enviable selection of independent boutiques, cafés, coffee shops, restaurants, bars and everyday shopping facilities. An excellent choice of schools, churches and sporting facilities further enhances the appeal of this wonderful location.\n\nFor those who appreciate the outdoors, the magnificent St Anne`s Park, renowned for its beautifully landscaped grounds and rose gardens, is close at hand, while the Bull Island and its celebrated Bird Sanctuary provide an extraordinary natural amenity on the doorstep of the city.\n\nExcellent transport connections ensure easy access to Dublin city centre and beyond, with both bus and DART services nearby. The IFSC, East Point Business Park, DCU, Dublin Airport, major hospitals and the M1 and M50 motorway networks are all readily accessible.\n\nRarely does a property of such inherent charm, generous proportions and outstanding potential become available in one of Clontarf`s most prestigious residential settings. Combining period character, mature gardens, excellent connectivity and significant scope to create a bespoke contemporary family residence, this is an opportunity of genuine distinction.\n\nViewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Reception Hallway - 4.03m (13'3\") x 1.8m (5'11\")\n\nLounge - 4.59m (15'1\") Into Bay x 3.64m (11'11\")\nFeature bay window. Attractive fireplace. Folding doors.\n\nDining Room - 4.86m (15'11\") x 3.63m (11'11\")\nWith feature fireplace\n\nFamily Room - 2.52m (8'3\") x 3.66m (12'0\")\nFrench doors leading out to the garden\n\nKitchen /Breakfast Room - 6.41m (21'0\") x 3.45m (11'4\") Irregular Shape\n\nRear hallway - 4.98m (16'4\") x 1.04m (3'5\")\nWith storage closets and hotpress. Attic access.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.63m (11'11\") x 4.01m (13'2\")\nTo the rear. Built in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 2 - 2.92m (9'7\") x 3.89m (12'9\")\nWith built in wardrobes\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.91m (9'7\") x 2.63m (8'8\")\nWith built in wardrobes\n\nBathroom - 2.53m (8'4\") x 1.66m (5'5\")\nComprising of bath, separate shower unit, wc and wash hand basin.\n\nGuest WC\nWith wash hand basin.\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
